# Migration checksums cover exact bytes (M1-SCHEMA.md, I2 and I10), so line
# endings are part of the identity of a migration. Without this pin, a checkout
# on a machine configured for CRLF rewrites every .sql file and the runner
# aborts on the next start with "migration has been edited" — correctly, and
# uselessly.
#
# Applies to every .sql file, not just migrations: a fixture that disagrees with
# its migration about line endings is its own kind of afternoon.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, narrower blast radius: fuzz seeds are compared byte for byte
# against inputs that once crashed a target.
fuzz/seeds/** -text
